Package: fish
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: xsel, python3, man-db
Description: friendly interactive shell
 fish is a smart and user-friendly command line shell for macOS, Linux and the
 rest of the family. It has autosuggestions from history and completions,
 syntax highlighting as you type, tab completions generated from man pages, and
 sane scripting with no arcane quoting rules — all working out of the box with
 no configuration.
 .
 This package repackages the statically linked musl binary published upstream.
 Since fish 4.0 the functions and completions that used to live in
 /usr/share/fish are embedded in the executable, so unlike the Debian archive
 build this package needs neither a fish-common data package nor any shared
 library at runtime.
